Package: mica-wifi-ap
Version: 2.12-mica1
Source-Date-Epoch: 1790380800
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Mica OS <hi@micaos.dev>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, libnl-3-200, libnl-genl-3-200, libssl3t64, iw, rfkill
Description: Mica OS Wi-Fi access point: a minimal hostapd
 /usr/sbin/hostapd and /usr/sbin/hostapd_cli compiled from the upstream
 hostap release with the nl80211 driver only, and WPA2 and WPA3 personal
 through the root's OpenSSL. No RADIUS, accounting or dynamic VLANs.
 .
 hostapd@.service is installed and not enabled: micad's access-point
 reconciler starts the instance for the interface it brought up and renders
 its /etc/hostapd/<interface>.conf. /etc is inside the read-only root, so
 etc-hostapd.mount binds /etc/hostapd from the STATE partition, where the
 AP pre-shared key also survives an A/B update.
 .
 Station support, and the regulatory database reload, is mica-wifi: a board
 with an access point installs both, and a station-only board installs no
 hostapd.
